  "body": "Closes #644\nClaim: cloud/i644-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i644-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (a216cab56f1f51d04)\n\n**Problem.** In light mode `--secondary` (108,108,112) is 4.45:1 on the classic whitelist header date (`--love`), 4.05:1 on the folded blocked-quote header inside a whitelisted message (classic) and 4.45:1 in modern (Mac check of #577, numbers in #644).\n\n**Cause.** `reader.css` draws `--secondary` text on `--love` and on a tint over `--love`; the colour was never adjusted for those surfaces.\n\n**Change.** One scoped token in `reader.css`: `.message.whitelist { --secondary-tinted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--secondary) 80%, var(--text)) }`, used for (a) the classic whitelist header `.date`, light only (in dark #1210 already draws it in `--text`, which stays), and (b) `table.quote-blocked b.s1` inside a whitelisted message, both styles. Light contrast: classic date 4.45 → 5.67, classic quote header 4.05 → 5.15, modern quote header 4.45 → 5.67; dark quote header 6.4 / 6.7. Follows themes. Not wider: other `--secondary` uses and the modern header date are untouched.\n\n**Tests.** New `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests` (real `WKWebView`): composites the ancestors' backgrounds under the header date and the blocked quote header and expects ≥ 4.5 in modern/classic × light/dark, plus the classic dark date still in the page text colour. Cloud (Linux) session: not run here, so not seen red; per Opus's recomputation three light assertions fail without the CSS (4.45, 4.05, 4.45). Compile check runs it. `swiftlint --strict` clean.\n\n**Follow-ups (not in this PR, same class, found by review):** a folded blocked quote inside a moderation message (`--modo`, light) has `--secondary` at 4.23:1; the date of a continuation of an allowlisted classic-light message is 3.28:1. Listed on #893 for the orchestrator to open as issues.\n\nDevice check owed: none beyond the next general review (#893).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGpzQVF7mCzgQw9cqk",
