   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, a1f0a4446643fa928, round 1)**\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5) : REQUEST CHANGES** — head 9c4fbea\n\n1. **High**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/ReaderWhitelistContrastWebTests.swift:12` and `:25`. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict` (`ci.yml:28`), and it reports 2 serious violations on this file: `inclusive_language` (the type name contains \"whitelist\") and `line_length` (141 > 140 on line 25). Lint goes red. Fix: rename the type (e.g. `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests`) and wrap line 25.\n2. **Medium**, `reader.css:323`. The new rule `.style-classic .message.whitelist .header .date` has specificity (0,5,0). In dark mode it beats #1210's `.style-classic .message .date { color: var(--text) }` (0,3,0, `reader.css:78`). On a classic-dark allowlisted message, the date drops from 13.5:1 to 7.1:1. On a continuation of that message (75 % opacity), it drops from 8.4:1 to 4.81:1 over the legacy grey and 4.63:1 over black, barely above AA. That undoes a deliberate dark decision. The comment's \"in dark the mix only raises the contrast\" is false: it compares against `--secondary`, but the date there was `--text`. The dark tests stay green (7.1 ≥ 4.5), so nothing guards against this. Fix: scope the line to light, or restate `color: var(--text)` for this selector inside the dark block, and test that dark keeps `--text`.\n3. **Low**, `reader.css:319-321`. The comment says the mix gives \"6.2 and 5.6 in light\". A recomputation with the probe's formula gives 5.67 (header) and 5.15 (blocked quote). Correct the numbers (L08).\n4. **Low**, neighbouring cases of the same class:\n   - A folded blocked quote inside a moderation message (`--modo`, light) puts `--secondary` at 4.23:1.\n   - A continuation of an allowlisted classic-light message puts the date at 3.28:1.\n\n   Cover them or open an issue.\n\n**Verified**\n- Read the diff against `reader.css`: specificity, the dark block, themes with `:where()`, and the `b.s1` rules.\n- Checked the test against `ReaderWebTestSupport`, the `ReaderRenderOptions` / `VisibilityPolicy` / `ReaderMessage` initializers and `QuoteMarkup.annotate`. The test should compile.\n- Recomputed every ratio in Python with the probe's formula. In light, the test should fail without the CSS (4.45 and 4.05).\n- Ran `swiftlint --strict`: 2 violations.\n- Not run: the WebKit tests (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
